Don';t give me answers, but we've effectively ruled out a write error and narrowed it to a caching issue

Yes, exactly.

At this point the graph has done something useful:

H1["Write error?"] is now mostly dead.

H2["Cache invalidation?"] is now the active investigation path.

O2["Event exists in database"] is stronger than just “no errors” because it shows the write happened.

One small terminology thing: O2 -->|refutes| H1 may be a little too strong unless the “event row” is exactly the thing that was supposedly failing to write. If it proves the save itself persisted, then fine. If it only proves some related row exists, then weakens may be more accurate.

But structurally, yes: you now have a narrowed investigation state, not a final answer. The next move is not “guess root cause,” but ask:

If caching is the live hypothesis, what observable would distinguish cache invalidation failure from read-path or frontend-state weirdness?

