Yes — and that’s a very useful twist for the framework.

It creates a distinction between:

suspected mechanism
updated_at not touched → invalidation skips eviction

and:

actual mechanism
TTL too long / wrong cache expiry policy → stale value survives longer than expected

So the graph should allow a hypothesis to be partially right but mechanistically wrong.

